## 💻 CODE GENERATION PATTERNS

### Task Structure Template
```yaml
- name: [Verb] [what] [optional context]
  [module_name]:
    [parameter]: [value]
    state: [present|absent|started|stopped]
  become: [yes|no]
  tags:
    - [tag1]
    - [tag2]
  when: [condition]
  changed_when: [condition for shell tasks]
  failed_when: [condition]
  notify: [handler_name]
```

### Error Handling Pattern
```yaml
- name: Task with comprehensive error handling
  block:
    - name: Main task
      [module]:
        [params]
  
  rescue:
    - name: Handle error
      debug:
        msg: "Error occurred: {{ ansible_failed_result }}"
    
    - name: Cleanup on failure
      [cleanup_task]
  
  always:
    - name: Always execute
      [always_task]
```

### Platform-Specific Pattern
```yaml
# tasks/main.yml
- name: Include distribution-specific tasks
  include_tasks: "{{ ansible_distribution | lower }}.yml"

# tasks/ubuntu.yml
- name: Ubuntu-specific tasks
  apt:
    name: package
    state: present

# tasks/fedora.yml
- name: Fedora-specific tasks
  dnf:
    name: package
    state: present
```

